# 🌤️⚡ Atmospheric Weather Forecast App

A responsive, real-time weather forecasting web application built as part of The Odin Project curriculum. This project focuses on asynchronous JavaScript (`async`/`await`), third-party REST API integration with Visual Crossing, clean data normalization, dynamic Webpack SVG asset bundling, and adaptive UI theming that shifts based on live weather conditions.

<p align="center">
  <img src="./odin-weather-app-preview.png" width="600" alt="Weather App Screenshot">
</p>

---

## ✨ Features

- **Real-Time Global Weather Search:** Fetches live current conditions and a 5-day forecast for any city worldwide via the Visual Crossing Timeline API.
- **Instant °C / °F Unit Toggle:** Caches fetched metric data in memory and converts temperatures (`°C` ↔ `°F`) and wind speeds (`km/h` ↔ `mph`) instantaneously without triggering redundant network requests.
- **Dynamic Weather Themes:** Automatically transitions the background gradient palette (`clear`, `cloudy`, `rain`, `snow`, and `night`) to match the active location's weather icon code.
- **Dynamic Webpack SVG Imports:** Resolves and bundles the full Visual Crossing color SVG icon set at runtime using Webpack dynamic `import()` expressions and parallel `Promise.all()` loading.
- **Loading & Error States:** Displays an animated loading spinner during API requests and clean error banners for invalid or unrecognized locations.

---

