## 🛠️ Technical Deep Dive

### Asynchronous API Fetching & Data Normalization

The API module separates network requests from UI rendering—fetching raw JSON from Visual Crossing and stripping away dozens of unused telemetry fields into a lean, predictable data object:

```
// src/weatherApi.js
export function processWeatherData(rawData) {
  const current = rawData.currentConditions;

  return {
    location: rawData.resolvedAddress,
    timezone: rawData.timezone,
    description: rawData.description,
    current: {
      tempC: current.temp,
      feelsLikeC: current.feelslike,
      humidity: current.humidity,
      windSpeedKmh: current.windspeed,
      conditions: current.conditions,
      icon: current.icon,
      datetime: current.datetime,
    },
    forecast: rawData.days.slice(0, 5).map((day) => ({
      date: day.datetime,
      tempMaxC: day.tempmax,
      tempMinC: day.tempmin,
      conditions: day.conditions,
      icon: day.icon,
      precipProb: day.precipprob,
    })),
  };
}
```

### Dynamic Webpack Asset Imports

Instead of hardcoding dozens of static icon imports, the DOM controller leverages Webpack's context module resolution via template-literal dynamic imports with a safe fallback:

```
// src/domController.js
async function loadWeatherIcon(iconName) {
  try {
    const iconModule = await import(`./icons/${iconName}.svg`);
    return iconModule.default;
  } catch {
    const fallbackModule = await import("./icons/clear-day.svg");
    return fallbackModule.default;
  }
}
```

---

## 🧱 CSS Styling & Dynamic Weather Themes

Glassmorphic cards (`backdrop-filter: blur(12px)`) sit atop smooth CSS gradient transitions driven by body classes mapped to Visual Crossing's icon codes:

```
/* src/styles.css */
body {
  font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif;
  min-height: 100vh;
  color: #ffffff;
  transition: background 0.5s ease;
}

body.theme-clear {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #1e88e5, #64b5f6);
}

body.theme-cloudy {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #546e7a, #90a4ae);
}

body.theme-rain {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #263238, #455a64);
}

body.theme-night {
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #0f172a, #1e293b);
}
```

