## 📁 File Structure

```
odin-weather-app/
├── dist/                   # Production-ready compiled bundle output
├── src/
│   ├── icons/              # Visual Crossing color SVG weather icon set
│   ├── domController.js    # UI rendering, unit conversions, themes, & icon loader
│   ├── index.js            # Application entry point, state, & event listeners
│   ├── styles.css          # Glassmorphic card layout & dynamic weather themes
│   ├── template.html       # Semantic HTML skeleton for HtmlWebpackPlugin
│   └── weatherApi.js       # Visual Crossing API client & JSON data processor
├── eslint.config.js        # ESLint flat configuration
├── .prettierrc             # Prettier code formatting rules
├── package.json            # Dependencies and npm scripts
├── webpack.config.js       # Webpack ESM bundling & dev-server configuration
└── Weather App Preview.jpg # Application preview screenshot
```

---

## 💻 Installation & Usage

1. Clone the repository
```
git clone https://github.com/Villa116/odin-weather-app.git
```

2. Navigate into the project directory
```
cd odin-weather-app
```

3. Install dependencies
```
npm install
```

4. Start the development server
```
npm run dev
```

5. Build for production
```
npm run build
```

---

## 🧪 Technologies Used

- **HTML5:** Semantic landmarks, accessible form inputs, and ARIA status/alert regions.
- **CSS3:** CSS Grid, Flexbox, backdrop-filter glassmorphism, keyframe spinner animations, and smooth background transitions.
- **JavaScript (ES6+):** `async`/`await`, Fetch API, `Promise.all()`, ES Modules (`import`/`export`), and dynamic `import()`.
- **Webpack 5:** Asset resource bundling, CSS/HTML loaders, `HtmlWebpackPlugin`, and live-reloading webpack-dev-server.
- **Visual Crossing Weather API:** RESTful timeline weather data and official weather SVG iconography.
- **ESLint & Prettier:** Automated code linting and consistent formatting.

---

## 🌟 Future Enhancements

- **Hourly Forecast Breakdown:** Add an interactive hourly timeline view for temperature and precipitation chances throughout the day.
- **Geolocation Auto-Detect:** Use the browser Geolocation API to load the user's local weather automatically on first visit.
- **Recent Searches & Favorites:** Persist recently searched cities in `localStorage` for one-click switching.

